  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/2e040bf3-e90e-4fb4-bca6-a284effb59ec-image.png\" style=\"width: 515px; height: 106px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d3145e92-ac07-4cca-82cf-f840306b946e-image.png\" style=\"width: 404px; height: 121px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3ed57e95-36dc-4c69-9ede-4bc01a8a0fc8-image.png\" style=\"width: 482px; height: 138px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/89451035-9b05-4bf1-894e-a840c4ead5f4-image.png\" style=\"width: 414px; height: 257px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>We know that drugs help us diagnose and cure numerous illnesses. But any drug consumed by humans can actually have two kinds of effects - therapeutic effects and side effects. The goal is to prescribe the ideal drug, the one that only has a therapeutic effect.</p>",
